#: DESCRIPTION.md:1
msgid "Permutationally Invariant Network for Enhanced Sampling (PINES)"
msgstr "Permutationally Invariant Network for Enhanced Sampling（PINES）"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:3
msgid ""
"PINES is a data-driven method for the automatic discovery of high variance "
"collective variables (CVs) and enhanced sampling to obtain free energy "
"landscapes of both single and multi-component molecular systems. It can be "
"conceived as a permutationally invariant extension to the Molecular Enhanced"
" Sampling with Autoencoders (MESA) method. PINES comprises three main "
"components:"
msgstr ""
"PINES は、分散が大きい Collective Variables（CVs）を自動的に発見し、Enhanced Sampling "
"によって単一成分・多成分の分子系の自由エネルギー地形を求める、Data-driven な手法である。Molecular Enhanced "
"Sampling with Autoencoders（MESA）法を Permutationally Invariant "
"に拡張したものと考えられる。PINES は、主に次の3つの要素からなる。"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:5
msgid "Components of PINES"
msgstr "PINES の構成要素"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:7
msgid ""
"**Permutation Invariant Vector (PIV) Featurization (F):** Provides a "
"translationally, rotationally, and permutationally invariant representation "
"of the molecular system."
msgstr ""
"**Permutation Invariant Vector（PIV）による Featurization（F）：** "
"分子系について、並進・回転・粒子の置換に対して不変な表現を与える。"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:10
msgid ""
"**Universal Function Approximators (Autoencoders):** Used for discovering "
"high-variance CVs {($\\xi_1$, $\\xi_2$, ...)} from the molecular dynamics "
"data."
msgstr ""
"**Universal Function Approximators（Autoencoders）：** MD データから、分散が大きい CVs "
"{($\\xi_1$, $\\xi_2$, ...)} を発見するために用いる。"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:13
msgid ""
"**Molecular Dynamics (MD) Simulations with CV Biasing:** Enhanced sampling "
"MD simulations are performed by biasing along the high-variance CVs learned "
"by autoencoders. This tutorial uses **Parallel-Bias Metadynamics (PBMetaD)**"
" for sampling, though any CV-enhanced sampling method can be employed."
msgstr ""
"**CV に Bias を加える Molecular Dynamics（MD）シミュレーション：** Autoencoders が学習した分散の大きい "
"CVs に沿って Bias を加え、Enhanced Sampling MD を実行する。このチュートリアルでは **Parallel-Bias "
"Metadynamics（PBMetaD）** を Sampling に用いるが、CV に基づく他の Enhanced Sampling "
"法も使用できる。"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:18
msgid ""
"<em>Figure 1: Overview of PINES for automatic discovery of high-variance CVs"
" and biasing the system using CV-enhanced sampling to overcome the sampling "
"challenges of MD simulations in determining free energy landscapes of both "
"single and multi-molecular systems. (a) We perform MD simulations to sample "
"the phase space of the system. The snapshot shows a representation of a NaCl"
" system configuration in water with Na, Cl, O, and H colored in yellow, "
"green, red, and white, respectively. (b) Representation of the system "
"configurations sampled during MD simulation in Cartesian space, where {xi, "
"yi, zi} represent the x, y, and z positions of atom i in the system. (c) "
"Conversion of the system configurations sampled during MD simulation to a "
"permutationally, rotationally, and translationally invariant representation "
"using PIVs. (d) Learning differentiable and high-variance nonlinear CVs "
"using autoencoders. We use a feed-forward network as a universal function "
"approximator for both the encoder and decoder parts of the autoencoders. (e)"
" Principal component analysis to align the manifold discovered using "
"autoencoders with the highest variance directions. (f) CV enhanced sampling "
"using PBMetaD or termination of PINES upon the convergence of discovered "
"CVs. Figure adapted from 10.1021/acs.jctc.3c00923, copyright ACS.</em>"
msgstr ""
"<em>図1：分散が大きい CVs を自動的に発見し、CV に基づく Enhanced Sampling で系に Bias を加える PINES "
"の概要。単一分子系・多分子系の自由エネルギー地形を求める際の MD の Sampling 上の課題を克服する。(a) 系の Phase Space を "
"Sampling するため、MD シミュレーションを行う。図は水中の NaCl 系の Configuration を示し、Na、Cl、O、H "
"をそれぞれ黄、緑、赤、白で表している。(b) MD で Sampling した Configurations を Cartesian Space "
"で表す。{xi, yi, zi} は、系の原子 i の x、y、z 座標を表す。(c) PIVs を用い、MD で Sampling した "
"Configurations を、粒子の置換・回転・並進に対して不変な表現へ変換する。(d) Autoencoders "
"を用いて、微分可能で分散が大きい非線形 CVs を学習する。Encoder と Decoder の両方に、Universal Function "
"Approximator として Feed-forward Network を用いる。(e) Principal Component Analysis "
"を行い、Autoencoders が発見した Manifold を分散が最大となる方向に整列させる。(f) PBMetaD による CV "
"Enhanced Sampling を行うか、発見した CVs が収束したら PINES を終了する。図は "
"10.1021/acs.jctc.3c00923 をもとに改変。著作権 ACS。</em>"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:23
msgid "Tutorial: NaCl Ion Pair Dissociation in Water"
msgstr "チュートリアル：水中の NaCl Ion Pair Dissociation"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:25
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we apply PINES to investigate the "
"**association/dissociation process of a NaCl ion pair in water**. This is a "
"classic system, where it is well known that the rearrangement of water "
"molecules in the solvation shell of ions plays a critical role in driving "
"the association or dissociation of NaCl. In other words, enhanced sampling "
"of association or dissociation of Na+ and Cl- ions in water may require "
"explicit biasing along water degrees of freedom.Traditional techniques "
"struggle with this, as they do not naturally handle the **permutational "
"symmetry** of water molecules, i.e., their indistinguishability."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは、PINES を用いて**水中の NaCl Ion Pair の Association／Dissociation "
"過程**を調べる。このよく研究された系では、Ion の Solvation Shell 内の水分子の再配置が、NaCl の Association や "
"Dissociation を駆動するうえで重要であることが知られている。言い換えると、水中の Na+ と Cl- の "
"Association／Dissociation を Enhanced Sampling するには、水の自由度に明示的に Bias "
"を加える必要がある場合がある。従来の手法は、水分子の**Permutational Symmetry**、すなわち "
"Indistinguishability を自然には扱えないため、これが難しい。"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:27
msgid "Why Use PINES?"
msgstr "PINES を使う理由"

#: DESCRIPTION.md:29
msgid ""
"PINES addresses the challenge of indistinguishable solvent molecules by "
"using **PIV representation**. This feature of PINES automatically removes "
"translational, rotational, and permutational variances, allowing us to "
"discover **solvent-inclusive high-variance CVs** efficiently. This leads to "
"more effective enhanced sampling for complex systems such as the "
"dissociation of NaCl."
msgstr ""
"PINES は、**PIV Representation** "
"を用いて、区別できない溶媒分子を扱う課題に対処する。並進・回転・粒子の置換による表現の変化を自動的に取り除くことで、**溶媒を含み、分散が大きい "
"CVs** を効率よく発見できる。その結果、NaCl の Dissociation などの複雑な系を、より効果的に Enhanced Sampling "
"できる。"

